// @@@ If the index is valid (non-negative and less than the size of the list), then for every position i greater than the index and less than the previous size of the list minus one, the element at position i in the updated list should either be null if the corresponding element in the old list at position i+1 was null, or it should be equal to the element at position i+1 in the old list.
